  "why": "The 24 ITF slots are the only numbering this framework uses (ADR-0002, ADR-0026). Receipts, telemetry tags, charters and HADES all carry the ITF slot. The 'rune' field exists for exactly one purpose: the COBOL kernel numbers the same 24 in the v1.0.0 order, and a call to rune_authorize or a read of a rotation table has to be translated into and out of that order. A rune number is never a name, never an identity and never appears in a receipt, a tag or a log line outside the kernel bridge. A reviewer who sees one there has found a bug.",
